# NLnet Foundation funding for ActivityPub software.
#
# Sources:
#   https://nlnet.nl/project/ — the "All projects" table filtered with the
#     page's own ActivityPub keyword search (retrieved 2026-11-04). Each row
#     becomes one ex:Funding whose id is that project's NLnet page. The /kbin
#     mobile grant is included too: the index groups it under /kbin and it is a
#     second grant for the same codebase.
#   The project pages themselves for the fund, the grant period, the project
#     title and the notes on how a grant maps to a codebase.
#
# Modelling: a grant is a qualified relation
# (https://patterns.dataincubator.org/book/qualified-relation.html). The
# ex:Funding instance *is* the NLnet project page, so the grant id (the page
# URL) and its qualifiers — ex:name, ex:fund, ex:startDate, ex:endDate — sit on
# one node. ex:funder names the funder (NLnet) and ex:recipient names the funded
# software (the doap:Project records in data/software.ttl).
#
# ex:funds is the binary shortcut for the same relation, stated once per
# funder/software pair at the end of the file: a software project funded more
# than once still gets a single edge, while each ex:Funding keeps its own grant
# period (Funkwhale, GoToSocial, Lemmy and others have several).
#
# NLnet is an ex:Organization, not a standards body: the grants point at it
# only through ex:funder, and it has an organization page in the UI.
#
# Dates: xsd:gYearMonth for the period printed on the project page; when the
# page has no period yet, the start year from the project index stays an
# xsd:gYear. Projects with neither carry none.
#
# ex:description appears only where the funded work needs a word of
# explanation, either because the page's title names the work rather than the
# codebase, or because the grant maps onto a codebase already funded above.
#
# Four ActivityPub search results have no single codebase to point at, so they
# have no grant here (see the end of the file).
#
# Seeded with `devbox run seed` (see devbox.json).

@prefix ex: <http://example.org#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

# NLnet Foundation. The grants below point here with ex:funder.
<https://nlnet.nl/> a ex:Organization ;
  ex:name "NLnet Foundation" ;
  ex:homepage <https://nlnet.nl/> ;
  ex:logo "/logos/nlnet.svg" .

